  "body": "`assets/machines/lathe.mch` (X 0..320, Z -615..0) and `millturn.mch` (X 0..650, Z -620..0) give Z as a one-sided band. The limit check reads machine limits in program coordinates through the work offset (`app::machine`), as found in #457. So any approach or clearance move in front of the face (program Z > 0) is probably reported as out of stroke, and posting is refused. This is the same flaw #457 fixed for the VMC and tilt-head files (PR #477).\n\nLathe X measured from the spindle centreline is a legitimate one-sided band in program coordinates; Z is the suspect.\n\nDone means: a lathe facing/turning job with a normal Z clearance in front of the face passes the stroke check on the built-in Lathe and Mill-turn, and a genuine over-travel still refuses by name.\n",
